      "text": "George Brecht: Events",
      "links": [],
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Drip Music\n\n\n\nFor single or multiple performance.\n\n\n\nA source of dripping water and an empty vessel are arranged\nso that the water falls into the vessel.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "1959",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "/images/concept/brecht/s-DripMusicTourette2003-s.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "width": "183",
      "height": "200",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Drip Music, Fluxversion 1\n\n\n\nFirst performer on a tall ladder pours water from a pitcher very slowly down into the bell of a French horn or tuba held in the playing position by a second performer at floor level.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "1959",
      "links": []
    },
    {
